#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:2
msgid "Active Directory"
msgstr "Active Directory"

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:15
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "Descripción general"

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:17
msgid ""
"Active Directory is Microsoft’s primary authentication service. It is widely"
" used in enterprise organizations and even in Microsoft cloud services. "
"While Active Directory also supports LDAP protocol support (which |morpheus|"
" can integrate with as well), |morpheus| includes a dedicated identity "
"integration type specifically for Active Directory. By integrating Active "
"Directory, |morpheus| administrators can fully offload the work of managing "
"the user lifecycle to Active Directory. Creating new users, applying roles "
"to users, updating basic user data, disabling users, and more can be handled"
" in Active Directory and automatically filtered down to |morpheus|. This "
"section includes an example integration walkthrough as well as additional "
"details on the integration feature set."
msgstr ""
"Active Directory es Microsoft’s primario authentication servicio. It es "
"widely used in enterprise organizations y incluso in Microsoft cloud "
"servicios. While Active Directory también supports LDAP protocolo support "
"(cual |morpheus| puede integrate con as well), |morpheus| includes un "
"dedicated identity integration tipo específicamente para Active Directory. "
"By integrating Active Directory, |morpheus| administrators puede fully "
"offload el work of managing el usuario lifecycle to Active Directory. "
"Creating nuevo users, applying roles to users, updating basic user datos, "
"disabling users, y más puede be handled in Active Directory y "
"automáticamente filtered down to |morpheus|. This sección includes un "
"ejemplo integration walkthrough así como adicional detalles on la "
"integración característica set."

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:19
msgid ""
"Caution should be used when integrating more than one Active Directory "
"identity source with the same |morpheus| Tenant. You must ensure the users "
"on each identity source are unique users or that the two domains use "
"different naming conventions for users."
msgstr ""
"Caution debería be used cuando integrating más than one Active Directory "
"fuente de identidad con el mismo |morpheus| Tenant. You debe ensure el "
"usuarios on cada fuente de identidad son unique users o que el two domains "
"use diferente naming conventions para users."

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:22
msgid "How It Works"
msgstr "Cómo funciona"

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:24
msgid ""
"In |morpheus|, identity sources (if used) are configured per Tenant. In "
"order to see an identity integration or create a new one, navigate to a "
"Tenant detail page (|AdmTen| > Selected Tenant) and click "
":guilabel:`IDENTITY SOURCES`. From this page we can add a new identity "
"source or click the pencil (|pencil|) icon next to an existing identity "
"source to view or edit it. Any configured identity source will apply to just"
" one Tenant and they cannot be shared. One scenario where this is especially"
" useful is in an MSP appliance where each Tenant is a siloed environment for"
" a specific customer. The customer's own existing Active Directory server "
"and groups can be leveraged to build |morpheus| user accounts with correct "
"role mapping automatically."
msgstr ""
"In |morpheus|, fuente de identidads (if used) son configurado per Tenant. In"
" order to see un identity integration o create un nuevo one, navigate to un "
"Tenant página de detalles (|AdmTen| > Selected Tenant) y click "
":guilabel:`FUENTES DE IDENTIDAD`. From este página we puede add un nuevo "
"fuente de identidad o click el pencil (|pencil|) icon siguiente to un "
"existente fuente de identidad to view o edit it. Any configurado fuente de "
"identidad será apply to solo one Tenant y they no puede be shared. One "
"scenario donde este es especially useful es in un MSP appliance donde cada "
"Tenant es un siloed entorno para un específico customer. The customer's own "
"existente Active Directory server y groups puede be leveraged to build "
"|morpheus| user accounts con correct role mapping automáticamente."

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:26
msgid ""
"When configuring an Active Directory integration in |morpheus|, AD groups "
"are mapped to |morpheus| roles. When the user logs in for the first time, "
"|morpheus| adds the new user account with correct name, email address, and "
"applies one or more roles depending on configuration. Going forward, "
"|morpheus| will sync down any changes to the user, including any role "
"changes based on changes to the user's associated AD groups or updated "
"passwords. Additionally, disabling a user in AD will prevent them from "
"accessing |morpheus|."
msgstr ""
"When configuring un Active Directory integration in |morpheus|, AD groups "
"son mapped to |morpheus| roles. When el usuario logs in para el primero "
"time, |morpheus| adds el nuevo user cuenta con correct nombre, email "
"dirección, y applies one o más roles dependiendo de configuración. Going "
"forward, |morpheus| será sync down cualquier cambios to el usuario, "
"including cualquier role cambios basado en cambios to el usuario's "
"associated AD groups o actualizado passwords. Adicionalmente, disabling un "
"usuario in AD será prevent them desde accessing |morpheus|."

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:28
msgid ""
"|morpheus| will connect over port 389 for non-secure LDAP and port 636 for "
"secure LDAP. Ensure that |morpheus| is able to talk to the AD server on the "
"proper port."
msgstr ""
"|morpheus| será connect over puerto 389 para non-secure LDAP y puerto 636 "
"para secure LDAP. Asegúrese de que |morpheus| es capaz de talk to el AD "
"server on el proper puerto."

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:31
msgid "Example Integration"
msgstr "Example Integration"

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:33
msgid ""
"In a simple example, we have an Active Directory server which has two groups"
" relevant to |morpheus|, \"Morpheus Users\" and \"Morpheus Admins.\" We will"
" configure |morpheus| so that only users in the \"Morpheus Users\" group can"
" access |morpheus| in any capacity. Users who are also in the \"Morpheus "
"Admins\" group will take on the System Admin role in |morpheus|. We'll see "
"later when the integration is configured how |morpheus| roles can be mapped "
"to AD groups. In the same AD server, I have two users. John Smith is in "
"groups \"Morpheus Users\" and \"Morpheus Admins\". John Jones is only in the"
" \"Morpheus Users\" group."
msgstr ""
"In un simple ejemplo, we tienen un Active Directory server cual tiene two "
"groups relevante to |morpheus|, \"Morpheus Users\" y \"Morpheus Admins.\" We"
" será configure |morpheus| so que solo users in el \"Morpheus Users\" group "
"puede acceso |morpheus| in cualquier capacity. Users quien son también in el"
" \"Morpheus Admins\" group será take on el System Admin role in |morpheus|. "
"We'll see later cuando la integración es configurado how |morpheus| roles "
"puede be mapped to AD groups. En el mismo AD server, I tienen two users. "
"John Smith es in groups \"Morpheus Users\" y \"Morpheus Admins\". John Jones"
" es solo in el \"Morpheus Users\" group."

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:36
msgid ".. image:: images/integration_guides/identity_sources/ad/ad.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/integration_guides/identity_sources/ad/ad.png"

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:37
msgid ""
"Knowing the AD scheme and the requirements for |morpheus| user roles, we can"
" begin the process of creating the integration. Identity integrations are "
"specific to each Tenant so begin by navigating to the Tenant detail page "
"(|AdmTen| > Selected Tenant) and clicking :guilabel:`IDENTITY SOURCES`. On "
"setting the type to \"Active Directory,\" the form will update with the "
"needed fields. Note the following basic fields:"
msgstr ""
"Knowing el AD scheme y el requirements para |morpheus| user roles, we puede "
"begin el proceso of creating la integración. Identity integrations son "
"específico to cada Tenant so begin by navigating to el Tenant página de "
"detalles (|AdmTen| > Selected Tenant) y clicking :guilabel:`FUENTES DE "
"IDENTIDAD`. On setting el tipo to \"Active Directory,\" el formulario será "
"update con el needed campos. Note el following basic campos:"

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:39
msgid ""
"**AD SERVER:** The IP address or hostname for the Active Directory Server"
msgstr ""
"**AD SERVER:** The IP dirección o hostname para el Active Directory Server"

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:40
msgid ""
"**DOMAIN:** The AD domain in which the relevant users and groups reside"
msgstr "**DOMAIN:** The AD domain in cual el relevante users y groups reside"

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:41
msgid ""
"**BINDING USERNAME:** A server user which has access to relevant objects on "
"the AD server. In my example, I've used the in-built Administrator user "
"which is the easiest option. Other users may be used depending on your "
"organization's IT security policies but the integration with |morpheus| will"
" not work properly if the user does not have the needed access"
msgstr ""
"**BINDING USERNAME:** A server user cual tiene acceso to relevante objetos "
"on el AD server. In my ejemplo, I've used el in-built Administrator user "
"cual es el easiest opción. Other users puede be used dependiendo de your "
"organization's IT security policies pero la integración con |morpheus| no "
"work properly if el usuario no tienen el needed acceso"

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:42
msgid "**BINDING PASSWORD:** The password for the user in the prior field"
msgstr ""
"**BINDING PASSWORD:** The contraseña para el usuario in el prior campo"

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:44
msgid ""
"With the basic configurations completed, the remaining configurations will "
"affect |morpheus| user and role generation. A REQUIRED GROUP is optional and"
" is a group the user *must* be in to have any |morpheus| access. Here we "
"require that users be in the \"Morpheus Users\" group. A DEFAULT ROLE is "
"required and will be assigned to all users regardless of any additional "
"roles they may be assigned based on their AD group membership. Beyond that, "
"all other |morpheus| roles will be listed here and an AD group name can be "
"associated with as many as you required. In this example, we are giving "
"users in the \"Morpheus Admins\" group the |morpheus| System Admin role. "
"Though we did not use them, it's worth pointing out that ENABLE ROLE MAPPING"
" PERMISSION will give administrators in the Tenant the ability to update the"
" AD role mappings (though they will not have access to the core integration "
"fields such as AD SERVER, DOMAIN, or binding user details). MANUAL ROLE "
"ASSIGNMENT allows users to manually update |morpheus| roles outside of the "
"automatic mappings created by the AD integration."
msgstr ""
"With el basic configurations completed, el remaining configurations será "
"affect |morpheus| user y role generation. A REQUIRED GROUP es opcional y es "
"un grupo el usuario *debe* be in to tienen cualquier |morpheus| acceso. Here"
" we require que users be in el \"Morpheus Users\" group. A DEFAULT ROLE es "
"requerido y será be assigned to todos users regardless of cualquier "
"adicional roles they puede be assigned basado en their AD group membership. "
"Beyond que, todos otro |morpheus| roles será be listed aquí y un AD group "
"nombre puede be asociado con as muchos as you requerido. In este ejemplo, we"
" son giving users in el \"Morpheus Admins\" group el |morpheus| System Admin"
" role. Though we did no use them, it's worth pointing out que ENABLE ROLE "
"MAPPING PERMISSION será give administrators in el Tenant el ability to "
"update el AD role mappings (though they no tienen acceso to el core "
"integration campos como AD SERVER, DOMAIN, o binding user detalles). MANUAL "
"ROLE ASSIGNMENT permite un los usuarios manualmente update |morpheus| roles "
"outside of el automático mappings creado by el AD integration."

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:47
msgid ".. image:: images/integration_guides/identity_sources/ad/intConfig.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: images/integration_guides/identity_sources/ad/intConfig.png"

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/active_directory.rst:48
msgid ""
"With the above integration steps completed, users can now log into "
"|morpheus| and a user account with correct roles will automatically be "
"created. In our example case, John Smith has logged in and we can see he is "
"assigned the default role as well as the System Admin role based on his AD "
"group associations. Going forward, |morpheus| will continue to sync any "
"changes to these users. For example, |morpheus| roles may be updated based "
"on changing AD groups or user access may be completely revoked by disabling "
"the user in AD."
msgstr ""
"With el anterior integration pasos completed, users puede ahora log en "
"|morpheus| y un usuario cuenta con correct roles será automáticamente be "
"creado. In our ejemplo case, John Smith tiene logged in y we puede see he es"
" assigned el predeterminado role así como el System Admin role basado en his"
" AD group associations. Going forward, |morpheus| será continue to sync "
"cualquier cambios to estos users. Por ejemplo, |morpheus| roles puede be "
"actualizado basado en changing AD groups o user acceso puede be completely "
"revoked by disabling el usuario in AD."

